ell young Rosie who's played  by Alexa Davies also brings some nice  little moments as well so you can really  look forward to seeing those two on  screen and the moment where young Tanya  tells young Sam that she visually enjoys  him is just priceless as for the  returning cast I cannot get enough of  Christine Baranski and Julie Walters as  Donna's friends and fellow dynamos Tanya  and Rosie beauty comes not only  exquisite structure of your bones and  left in your sparkling eyes but from the  goodness that flowers within you like a  fountain  I've been washed and brought to my tent  I don't think fountains flower did that  remind us and then there's a hilarious  way they sing angel eyes to Sophie with  christine baranski  tanya hardly letting julie walters rosie  get a word in edgeways  of course the prequel aspect of this  film means there are obviously fewer  scenes with the original cast which of  course is a bit of a shame because  they're all so great so for example  while we do see Colin Firth stellan  skarsgård and Pierce Brosnan sing dance  and act we do see them doing less of  that than we did in the first film  speaking of the original cast someone I  would have loved to have seen much more  of is Meryl Streep astana I just adored  scenes Streep singing dancing and acting  with gusto in the first film and I  really did miss her here now while we  certainly don't get enough Meryl Streep  in the movie we do get the added benefit  of cher in a role that was written  specifically for her and which fits her  like a glittery glove is it a touch  insane that sure he's only three years  older than Meryl Streep in real life  it's playing Donna's mother of course it  is  do I care absolutely not because at the  end of the day we get to hear Sher Singh  Fernando complete with a big fireworks  display and we get some crazy moments  with Sophie's grandma now when it comes  to the music obviously in the first film  we got an absolute turn of Abbas biggest  greatest hits which means that in this  film we get some lesser-known Abba  tracks like when I kiss the teacher why  did it have to be me kisses of fire and  undone taen Dante I've been waiting for  you and my love my life but we do also  get some songs that weren't in the  original film that you will I think  definitely recognize there's the name of  the game which is performed by Lily  James there's knowing me knowing you  which is again Lily James and Jeremy  Irvin and there's also angel eyes and  Fernando as well and not to worry  because we do still get many of the  hugely popular hits from the first film  so there's Mamma Mia dancing Queens  super trouper and Waterloo to name a few  for dancing Queen we get a flotilla of  fishermen along with stellan skarsgård  and Colin Firth recreating the Titanic  pose as they sail to  Island and for Waterloo it's in a  Parisian restaurant with a young Harry  and Donna and we even get an Abba cameo  as well with Benny playing the piano and  Mamma Mia gets a spirited performance by  the young dynamos this time when the  film proper ends we get a fantastic  version of Super Trouper with all the  main cast joining in  while Super Trouper was amazing I was a  little bit disappointed that we only got  one song and dance routine in the kind  of curtaincall cast party moment in the  film this time around because last time  if you remember we got two songs we got  dancing Queen and Waterloo so it would  have been fantastic if we just got one  more now if you stay to the very end of  the credits after everyone's names  rolled by we do get a little unexpected  extra something with an unexpected post  credits scene which makes up a little  bit for only one extra song after the  film finishes the post credits scene  features comic actor homage Lili as the  Greek official who was checking people's  passports before they boarded the Island  Ferry earlier in the film if you  remember he had quite a few opinions  about what people look like in their